<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Your venue has a tablet (a <em>clock-in terminal</em>) where you clock in when you start a shift and
        clock out when you finish.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="With your PIN">
        <ol>
            <li>On the tablet, tap your name. Everyone on the rota there today is listed.</li>
            <li>Type your 4 to 6 digit clock-in PIN.</li>
            <li>The tablet confirms you're clocked in. Do the same to clock out.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Set your PIN in the <strong>Clock-in PIN</strong> section of your <a href="/account/manage">account page</a>. Your manager
            can also set it for you. Keep it to yourself.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="With your phone">
        <ol>
            <li>Make sure you're signed in to Lanyard on your phone.</li>
            <li>Scan the QR code under <strong>Or scan with your phone</strong> on the tablet.</li>
            <li>Your phone confirms you're clocked in or out.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            The code changes every 30 seconds. If your phone says it has expired, scan the one showing now.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="If it won't let you clock in">
        <ul>
            <li>You can clock in from shortly before your shift starts. Your venue sets how early (an hour unless they've changed it).</li>
            <li>You need a published shift at that venue. If you're covering someone without being on the rota,
                ask a manager to add your time.</li>
            <li>If you forget to clock in or out, tell your manager. They can correct your time on the timesheet.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>See the time you've clocked on the <strong>My hours</strong> tab.</FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
